{"explanation":"A Galton board turns repeated left-or-right choices into a distribution: after 8 rows, a ball lands in bin k if it went right exactly k times. If each bounce independently goes right with probability p, then P(K = k) = C(8, k)p^k(1 − p)^(8 − k). Watch the blue experimental bars approach the gold theoretical marks as more balls fall; drag the bias handle to see how changing p shifts the distribution.","manimCode":"const rows = 8;
const centerX = -3;
const spacing = 0.46;
const pegTop = 1.8;
const rowGap = 0.4;
let probability = 0.5;
let counts = Array(9).fill(0);
let total = 0;
let busy = false;
let epoch = 0;

const title = new Text({ text: 'Galton board → binomial distribution', fontSize: 30, color: WHITE });
title.moveTo([0, 3.3, 0]);
